ETHNICITY
The last census enables a widespread and extensively study of population ethnicity. In the census
results, ethnic groups which has population less than 100 persons was categorized as “other”. Khalkh
ethnic group makes 83.8 percent of Mongolian population, increased by 1.4 percentage points from the
previous census, and followed by Kazakhs, 3.8 percent. The percentage of Durvuds, Bayads, and Buriads
declined from 2010.
